.TH FCLOSE 3S
.SH NAME
fclose, fflush \- close or flush a stream
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B "#include <stdio.h>"
.sp
.B "fclose(stream)"
.B "FILE *stream;"
.sp
.B "fflush(stream)"
.B "FILE *stream;"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fclose
causes any buffers for the named
.I stream
to be emptied, and the file
to be closed.
Buffers allocated by the standard input/output system are
freed.
.PP
.B fclose
is performed automatically upon calling
.BR exit (2).
.PP
.B fflush
causes any buffered data for the named output
.I stream
to be written
to that file.
The stream remains open.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
close(2), fopen(3), setbuf(3)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
These routines return
.B EOF
if
.I stream
is not associated with an output file,
or if buffered data cannot be transferred to that file.
.sp
